<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Project Sdk="Dalamud.NET.Sdk/15.0.0">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- First public build. The cleaning half is exercised daily; the organizer half has not been through a
         full in-game pass yet, so this stays below 1.0 until it has. -->
    <Version>0.12.1.0</Version>
    <Author>Raiden Shinryu</Author>
    <Name>Gleam</Name>
    <!-- Written the way the most-installed plugins write theirs: what it does, how, the commands, then what it
         needs. The installer shows this as plain text, so no markdown, and no semicolons, colons or dashes. -->
    <Punchline>Clears out your junk and puts the rest away.</Punchline>
    <Description>Gleam finds the junk in your bags, armoury chest, saddlebag, retainers and glamour dresser, and clears it out with one button. You choose whether it puts things up on the market board, sells them to vendors or discards them.

- Shows you everything first. Nothing leaves your bags until you press Clean.
- Layouts put the rest away, such as materia to the saddlebag and spare gear to a retainer.
- Hands-free trips walk to your retainers, the dresser and a merchant for you.
- Statistics show everything it has cleared.

Commands

/gleam
    Opens or closes Gleam. /gl does the same.
/gleam organize
    Opens the layouts that put things away.
/gleam stats
    Shows your statistics.
/gleam history
    Lists everything Gleam has cleaned or moved.
/gleam settings
    Opens the settings.
/gleam scan
    Looks through your inventory again.
/gleam merge
    Merges split stacks.
/gleam stop
    Stops whatever Gleam is doing.
/gleam selftest
    Checks what Gleam can find in the game without touching anything.
/gleam report
    Copies a bug report to your clipboard.
/gleam troubleshoot
    Opens the troubleshooting window.

Requires vnavmesh, and Lifestream to travel between towns. Gleam automates game actions, so use it at your own risk.</Description>
    <RepoUrl>https://github.com/sleousis/Gleam</RepoUrl>
    <!-- Shown beside the plugin in Dalamud's installer. Served from the repository itself so there is no
         second place to keep it in step. -->
    <IconUrl>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sleousis/Gleam/main/src/Gleam/images/icon.png</IconUrl>
    <Tags>inventory;cleanup;retainer;saddlebag;marketboard;organize;qol</Tags>
    <RootNamespace>Gleam</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Gleam</AssemblyName>
    <LangVersion>14.0</LangVersion>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <!--
      Pin the output path. Without this MSBuild appends the platform whenever it is not AnyCPU, so building
      the solution (which maps this project to x64) wrote bind\Release while building the project alone
      wrote bin\Release. The dev plugin loads one of them, so the other silently went stale.
    -->
    <OutputPath>bin\$(Configuration)\</OutputPath>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Gleam.Core\Gleam.Core.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Read by the "what's new" card, so release notes are written once, in CHANGELOG.md. -->
    <EmbeddedResource Include="..\..\CHANGELOG.md" LogicalName="Gleam.CHANGELOG.md" Visible="false" />
    <Content Include="Data\curated.json">
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
      <Visible>true</Visible>
    </Content>
    <Content Include="images\*.png">
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
      <Visible>true</Visible>
    </Content>
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
